{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Did I not say to you, saying: Do not sin against the child, and you did not listen.</b> The meaning is: I said to you at the time of the deed that you should not sin against him, for he is a child, and because of his youth he sinned against you, and it is fitting for you to overlook his offense." "<b>And also his blood.</b> The cruelty that you had at the time you cast him into the pit — behold, it is called to account, for even though you did not kill him with your hands, HaShem, may He be exalted, will demand his blood from you, and the deed is reckoned to you as though you had spilled his blood, for perhaps he had already died, being a child of play, unable to travel a road on his feet. Thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:53.653039922Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}